! Timing microbenchmark for the instruction unit (docs/
! microarchitecture_plan.md stage 2b): a two-instruction loop, NOP then
! count-and-branch back to it, taken ten times, then falling through
! to the halt. Performance Characteristics vol.1: LCI 2.4 + dec 0.6 =
! 3.0 us = 10 clocks (table 5); NOP 1.2 + 0.6 = 6 clocks (table 7); CB
! successful 4.2 + 0.6 = 16 clocks, unsuccessful 3.6 + 0.6 = 14
! (table 8). Budget: 10 + 10*(6+16) + 6 + 14 = 250 clocks, plus the
! first instruction fetch from memory (~7) and the halt instruction's
! own preparation. The CYCLES<= bound in run_tests.sh (280) is set
! from that arithmetic, not from a measurement, so it fails if the
! model's CB or NOP time drifts from the tables. (A branch to its own
! address halts this model, so the loop cannot be a lone CB.)
START   LCI, $1, 11         ! count 11: ten taken branches, then fall through
LOOP    NOP, 0.0
        CB, $1, LOOP        ! branch back while count != 0
DONE    BEW, $              ! halt
        END, START
